    "title": "Stormwater Pump Room",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "simetro",
    "description": "An urban stormwater facility where debris filters, lift stations, and retention basins must keep streets clear during flash-flood events, all while maintaining discharge compliance.",
    "tags": [
      "sl1",
      "scenario_language_v1",
      "stormwater",
      "water",
      "infrastructure",
      "easy",
      "draft"
    ],
    "palette_note": "Water and flood palette: dark background, neutral foreground, deep blue stormwater, teal filtered, cyan pumped, green basin, amber compliance. Evokes municipal water ops.",
    "layout_note": "Six SL1 places form a collection-to-outfall pipeline: rain collector top-left, debris filter, pump station center, retention basin right, discharge outfall far right, operations center above.",
    "node_language_note": "Place roles: source=rain-collector, processor=debris-filter/pump-station, buffer=retention-basin, dashboard=discharge-outfall, operator=operations-center.",
    "mover_path_note": "No legacy movers; SL1 links carry fluid flows. Six links span collector-to-outfall plus two bidirectional control buses.",
    "review_note": "Draft pending SL1 renderer. Schema validates. Easy difficulty adds flood-pressure events."
  },
